# Prototype modals

When adding or changing a form dialog (title + inline close, body, Cancel/Save), start from `_prototypes/shared/ui/proto-modal.js` and `proto-modal.css`. Do not copy overlay/open/close code from CST or Territories.

- Markup and `createProtoModal()` contract are documented at the top of `proto-modal.js`.
- Confirmation dialogs use `createProtoConfirmModal()` in `proto-confirm-modal.js`. Pass `host` to cover a parent modal; omit it to cover the viewport.
- Overlay clicks do not close dialogs. Pass `shouldCloseOnOverlay: true` to opt in.
- Put the X in `.proto-modal-header` next to the title. Never as a sibling above the form.
- Unique body content stays in the feature. Shared chrome (overlay, card, header, fields, check groups, notices, footer) does not.
- Info callouts use `.proto-modal-notice` (optional `.proto-modal-divider` above). Do not copy CST sender-notice styles into a feature.
- Radio and checkbox stacks in dialogs use `.proto-modal-check-group` / `.proto-modal-check`. Do not reuse `.filter-check-group` / `.filter-check` inside proto-modals.
- Profile-style cards (centered hero, no title row) still use `createProtoModal()` for open/close; keep `.profile-modal-close` in the corner.
- Existing pages may still use `profile-modal-*` / `target-modal-*` aliases. New dialogs should use `proto-modal-*`.
